      "id": 1,
      "text": "Springtown was originally called Littleton Springs by settler Joseph Ward before being renamed in the mid‑1870s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springtown%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office opened in 1875, and it was officially incorporated in 1884.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springtown%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1884 the College Hill Institute opened, making Springtown a regional education hub for a decade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://springtown.net/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic downtown streets now host live music, artisan vendors, and family‑friendly food, reflecting the town’s vibrant heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.springtownchamber.org/history/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Springtown Tabernacle, a cherished landmark, stands at the heart of the community and symbolizes unity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.springtownchamber.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Springtown sits in northeastern Parker County, about 25 miles northwest of downtown Fort Worth, surrounded by rolling oak and elm hills.",
